#: admin/settings-page-output.php:171
msgid "Utilities"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:181
msgid "Comments system removal"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:182
msgid "It will disable comments system completely; also set proper redirections and removes admin pages for comment managament."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:183
msgid "%1$sWARNING:%2$s If you're connected to external comment systems like Disqus via native comment support (for example, by installing official Disqus plugin), it will also remove/disable that connection."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:185
msgid "Disable built-in Wordpress comment system?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:191
msgid "Widgets removal"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:192
msgid "It will remove native widgets system (Appearance admin menu tab)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:195
msgid "Remove widget support?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:201
msgid "oEmbed restriction"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:202
msgid "It will disable oEmbed on site, while keeping it enabled for external platforms/apps."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:205
msgid "Restrict oEmbed?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:211
msgid "Self-pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:212
msgid "Disables self-pingbacks, after new posts creation or on-site linking."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:215
msgid "Disable self-pingbacks?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:221
msgid "Image Processing engine"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:222
msgid "WordPress is using Imagick by default, if available - this option forces usage of GD, which is generally faster. The downside is, that it supports a lot less image formats and image quality may drop."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:223
msgid "%1$sWARNING:%2$s Since GD PHP extension requires additional configuration for webp/avif formats, those may not be available to use, for plugins like CompressX or even natively processed in media library."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:226
msgid "Force GD Image Processing engine?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:232
msgid "Tags taxonomy removal"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:233
msgid "It will remove native tags taxonomy from default post type (Posts->Tags admin menu tab).%3$s Many non-blogs websites don't need those at all."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:234
msgid "%1$sWARNING:%2$s If you have any tags indexed and at least some traffic comes through those - this option can affect your position at search engines like Google."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:237
msgid "Unregister default tags taxonomy?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:243
msgid "Author archives"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:244
msgid "Authors archive pages can be considered redundant on installations, where posts are not categorized by WP users (as authors). %3$s Since author archives are part of WP Core and can't be \"removed\" per se, this function is limited to:%3$s 1. redirection of any author archive page queries to homepage (301 redirect); %3$s 2. removal of any author's links from functions like author_link\\the_author_posts_link; %3$s 3. removal of author's from native sitemaps (if it's actively used). %3$s Note: Most of the times, author's archives indexation or handling can be configured in settings of most of the popular SEO plugins. "
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:245
msgid "%1$sWARNING:%2$s If you have any author pages indexed and those are considered vital for your website blog categorization - this option can affect your position at search engines like Google."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:248
msgid "Disable author archives?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:254
msgid "WordPress Heartbeat API"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:255
msgid "The Heartbeat API is used for autosaving, post locking, and other real-time features. Increasing the interval reduces server load but may cause issues on functionalities, that heavily relies on Heartbeat API."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:256
msgid "Reduces server requests and CPU usage on both frontend and backend."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:258
msgid "Modify WordPress Heartbeat interval?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:259
msgid "Interval (seconds):"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:264
msgid "Default: 15 seconds. Range: 1-3600 seconds (1 hour)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:265
msgid "%1$sWARNING:%2$s Be VERY careful, when changing that interval, it could brake some essential functionalities on your website."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:271
msgid "Revisions"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:272
msgid "This option allows to change global number of revisions (including all post types, that actually supports revisions) per post/page. By default WordPress do not limit revisions number in any way and this usually makes database way bigger, than it should be - especially on content-heavy websites like blogs; this leads to worse website load times.%3$s How it works:%3$s %1$s-1 / Off%2$s - Default, no limit on revisions.%3$s %1$s0%2$s - revisions are disabled. %3$s %1$s1-999%2$s - revisions number for all posts type are limited to this number.%3$s Note: revisions WON'T be removed right away, once this option is enabled - you need to update specific post/page, to have it's revisions removed.%3$s If you want to clear your installation off revisions globally, then try using plugins like \"WP-Sweep\" or \"Optimize Database after Deleting Revisions\""
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:273
msgid "Reduces load on database and it's size on the long run."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:275
msgid "Modify global revisions number?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:276
msgid "Revisions:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:281
msgid "Default: -1 (unlimited). Range: 1-99."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page-output.php:282
msgid "%1$sWARNING:%2$s This option is not designed to override specific post type capabilities - if it doesn't support revisions, then this option won't change it in any way."
msgstr ""

